"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — is fixed value by binary search). If there is some good segment, you should update boundaries of binary search correctly. After that, it's very simple to restore answer. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://www.topcoder.com/tc?d1=tutorials&d2=lowestCommonAncestor&module=Static"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Some information about Sparce Table"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Авторское решение: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/359/submission/4968587"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4968587"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/359/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"359E - Neatness"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You should write recursive function, that will turn on the light in all rooms, where it's possible. Also this function will visit all rooms, which it may visit. Let this function is called paint(x, y), where x, y is the current room. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Paint"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") will use following idea: Let's look at all neighbors. If there is a light in the current direction (rule 3 from the statement), and the room ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ny"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") (current neighbor) has not yet visited, we will call our recursive function from ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ny"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Also, we will turn